body:
Review this synthetic web server configuration for the fictional site www.neoncorp.example.

```text
server_tokens off;
ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
location /static/ { expires 7d; }
location /backups/ { autoindex on; }
add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff;
```

Which directive creates the most direct information-exposure risk?

Review this vendor-neutral synthetic storage policy for the fictional account acct-000000-demo.

```text
{
  "resource": "bucket/neoncorp-invoices",
  "statements": [
    { "effect": "allow", "principal": "role/billing-app", "actions": ["object:read", "object:write"] },
    { "effect": "allow", "principal": "*", "actions": ["object:read", "object:list"] }
  ],
  "encryption": "enabled",
  "access_logging": "enabled"
}
```

Which element causes the biggest exposure?
